# GreeterWindow: shared actions of every login style (preview, mock password "tessera").
# NOTE: $TESSERA_BIN must point at the Rust binary; stderr "greeter (dry): ..." lines are MANUAL.
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo users &
wait 2
shot first
note Glass greeter with the first of 3 people chosen.
key -k Down
wait 0.5
shot down
note Down: next person (name and avatar change, field empty).
key -k Up
wait 0.5
key -k Up
wait 0.5
shot up-wrap
note Up from the first person wraps to the LAST person (and Down from the last wraps to the first).
key abc
wait 0.3
key -k Down
wait 0.5
shot field-cleared
note After typing abc and pressing Down the field is empty and the next person is chosen.
key -k Tab
wait 0.5
shot session
note Tab changed the session text under the field ("Hyprland  ▾" ... next); wraps after the last.
# Power: needs a click on the Shut Down button
ptr move 1060 1010 sleep 200 click down up
# NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness; the Shut Down button is at the bottom (guess x=1060,y=1010), compare with the shot.
wait 0.5
shot power-chosen
note Shut Down button turned red and the line says "Shut Down: click it again or press Return. Esc cancels."
key -k Escape
wait 0.5
shot power-cancelled
note Esc dropped the power choice; the line is back to normal and the window stays.
# MANUAL: click Shut Down twice: stderr shows "greeter (dry): poweroff"; choose Restart then Return: dry reboot logged
# Name edit
ptr move 960 480 sleep 200 click down up
wait 0.5
shot name-edit
note Clicking the name turned it into a username field with the name selected.
key grace
key -k Return
wait 0.6
shot grace
note That person is chosen (picture/initial changes) and focus is in the password field.
key -k Escape
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
